@misc{snowball_00082,
  abstract = {This is the replication package for our paper "Requirements Traceability Link Recovery via Retrieval-Augmented Generation".This package contains the source code, the dataset used in the evaluation, and the results of the evaluation. Requirements Java JDK 21 + Maven 3 OpenAI subscription: API Key Ollama Instance Structure of this Repository / : Contains the source code of the approach(Note: The most recent version of the tool can be found at ArDoCo/LiSSA-RATLR) /cache : Contains the cache for the evaluation. /configs : Contains the configurations used in the evaluation. /datasets : Contains the datasets used in the evaluation and the results of the evaluation. /results-r2r : Contains the results of the evaluation. /experiments : Contains the aggregated results of our experiments, as well as the scripts and results of the statistical tests. Installation You can use the provided JAR. Alternatively, build the project using Maven: mvn package The JAR will be created in the target folder (e.g., target/ratlr-*-jar-with-dependencies.jar). Usage Create a .env file based on the provided template. Run the JAR from the top-level directory: java -jar target/ratlr-*-jar-with-dependencies.jar eval -c ./configs/req2req/<<DesiredConfig>> Results of Evaluation All results are available in the results-r2r folder. Results are stored as Markdown (MD) files in the respective projects. Each file includes the configuration and the results of the evaluation. Example configuration: { "cache_dir" : "./cache/CCHIT", "gold_standard_configuration" : { "hasHeader" : true, "path" : "./datasets/req2req/CCHIT/answer.csv" }, "source_artifact_provider" : { "name" : "text", "args" : { "artifact_type" : "requirement", "path" : "./datasets/req2req/CCHIT/high" } }, "target_artifact_provider" : { "name" : "text", "args" : { "artifact_type" : "requirement", "path" : "./datasets/req2req/CCHIT/low" } }, "source_preprocessor" : { "name" : "artifact", "args" : {} }, "target_preprocessor" : { "name" : "artifact", "args" : {} }, "embedding_creator" : { "name" : "openai", "args" : { "model" : "text-embedding-3-large" } }, "source_store" : { "name" : "custom", "args" : {} }, "target_store" : { "name" : "custom", "args" : { "max_results" : "4" } }, "classifier" : { "name" : "mock", "args" : {} }, "result_aggregator" : { "name" : "any_connection", "args" : { "source_granularity" : "0", "target_granularity" : "0" } }, "tracelinkid_postprocessor" : { "name" : "identity", "args" : { "reverse" : "false" } } } Statistics # TraceLinks (GS): 587 # Source Artifacts: 116 # Target Artifacts: 1064 Results True Positives: 92 False Positives: 372 False Negatives: 495 Precision: 0.1983 Recall: 0.1567 F1 Score: 0.1751},
  author = {Hey, Tobias and Fuchß, Dominik and Keim, Jan and Koziolek, Anne},
  date = {2025},
  doi = {10.5281/zenodo.14779457},
  note = {Snowball round: 1; directions: backward; sources: OpenCitations Index v2; seed records: merged_1266: Requirements Traceability Link Recovery via Retrieval-Augmented Generation},
  title = {Replication Package for "Requirements Traceability Link Recovery via Retrieval-Augmented Generation"},
